course: dictionary
lesson: 6989
title: Papermaking: a craft with a long history
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Word parts can give you clues. The ending -making means making something, as in «papermaking», so papermaking is the craft of making paper. Like water or sand, it is an uncountable noun, so we do not say "a papermaking."
explain: The sentences give more clues about the process. «Cai Lun, an official of the Han court, improved papermaking about 1,900 years ago, using tree bark, old rags and fishing nets.» The things he used are the materials that paper is made from.
explain: Papermaking is also a big industry today, and it uses a lot of trees and water. «Recycled papermaking» means using old paper again, which helps to save trees. When you meet a new word, ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Papermaking means the craft or industry of making paper.
fact: Papermaking usually uses wood pulp, cotton, rags or recycled paper that has been soaked in water.
fact: The mixture is pressed into thin sheets and then dried.
fact: Papermaking was invented in China about two thousand years ago, and it is traditionally credited to Cai Lun.
fact: «Muslims learned papermaking from China and built paper mills in Baghdad, so books became cheaper.»
exercise: What does papermaking mean? | The craft of writing books | Selling paper in shops | *The craft of making paper | Cutting down trees for fires
exercise: «Recycled papermaking» uses old paper again. Why is recycling helpful? | It stops paper from drying | It makes trees grow faster | It makes paper more expensive | *It saves trees and water
exercise: The ending -making in papermaking is a clue. What does it tell you? | It is a question | *It is about making something | It is about a place | It means very old
test: Where was papermaking first invented, according to the lessons? | Spain | Baghdad | Egypt | *China
test: «Cai Lun improved papermaking using tree bark, old rags and fishing nets.» Which material is NOT named in this sentence? | Old rags | *Plastic bottles | Fishing nets | Tree bark
exam: Which option best describes papermaking? | Cutting trees into planks | *Making thin sheets of paper from materials such as wood pulp and rags | Painting pictures on card | Writing stories with a pen
